    factory, response writer, registrar client functions, monitoring entry
    point, agent-connection TLS context builder, tenant HTTP client class, and
    asyncio.ensure_future) before driving the entry points, those entry points
    can only be reached through code that resolves those collaborators via the
    module attributes named above.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner spawns two driver programs as subprocesses (the same
  interpreter, a JSON configuration passed as the single command-line
  argument). The drivers — not part of the implementation — import the
  application modules in-process, generate fresh sentinel credentials and
  certificates on every run, install the recording substitutes described above
  (a substitute database session supporting query().filter_by().count(),
  add(), commit(); a substitute registrar client; a substitute response
  writer; a substitute monitoring recorder; a substitute tenant HTTP client
  whose post returns an object exposing status_code, text, and json()), invoke
  the entry points, and print a single JSON report line that the runner
  parses. The driver programs, every substitute object, the stub tpm2_startup,
  and the shipped keylime configuration file all belong to the calling side;
  the engineer does not rebuild any of them.
