## Reached at
  A command-line executable at the absolute path `/app/qpdf/build/qpdf`, reached
  by callers as a subprocess:
      [QPDF_PATH] + list(args)   where QPDF_PATH = "/app/qpdf/build/qpdf"
  The binary is built during the image build from the QPDF 6.0.0 source tree
  staged into `/app` (`./autogen.sh && ./configure && make`). It is the project'"'"'s
  own artifact, not a preinstalled system tool. Callers depend on the working
  directory only insofar as the subprocess is launched with `cwd` unset; the
  executable itself is resolved by absolute path. A symlink `/usr/local/bin/qpdf`
  is also produced by the image build but callers use the absolute build path.

## Must provide
  A single executable responding to these CLI forms:
    --version                       flag
    --check                         flag, taking one PDF file path operand
    --show-object=N                 option (N is an object number), one PDF file path operand
    --linearize                     flag, two file path operands (in, out)
    --check-linearization           flag, one PDF file path operand
    <infile> <outfile>              two file path operands, no flag (rewrite)

## Called as
  subprocess.run([QPDF_PATH, ...args], capture_output=True, timeout=<n>, preexec_fn=<fn>)
  Each call is the argv list `/app/qpdf/build/qpdf` followed by zero or more
  flags/options and exactly the operands named below. Inputs are passed only as
  process arguments; nothing is read from stdin by callers.
    ["--version"]
        operands: none
    ["--check", <pdf_path>]
        <pdf_path> — 2nd argv element; a path string
    ["--show-object=3", <pdf_path>]
        1st argv element is the literal option string; <pdf_path> — 2nd argv
        element; a path string
    ["--linearize", <in_path>, <out_path>]
        <in_path> — 2nd argv element; a path string. <out_path> — 3rd argv
        element; a path string
    ["--check-linearization", <pdf_path>]
        <pdf_path> — 2nd argv element; a path string
    [<in_path>, <out_path>]
        <in_path> — 1st argv element after the program; a path string.
        <out_path> — 2nd argv element; a path string

## Setup required
  The executable must exist at `/app/qpdf/build/qpdf` and be executable. Callers
  create the PDF file paths they pass as operands in the system temporary
  directory and remove them afterward; those files are caller-owned, not part of
  the implementation. The QPDF build is performed during image construction, so
  the artifact is expected to already be present at the reached-at path when the
  caller runs.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner launches the executable as a subprocess via `subprocess.run`
  using the absolute path above, capturing stdout and stderr. The runner also
  assembles the PDF operands it passes to the executable and owns their
  lifecycle — the PDF-building helpers, the temporary-file creation, and the
  cleanup belong to the calling side, not to the implementation. The runner is
  invoked through a shell script that installs a Python package manager and
  pytest, then runs pytest; that script is also part of the calling side.
```

