- **Required interface:**
  ```c
  GF_Err mpgviddmx_configure_pid(GF_Filter *filter, GF_FilterPid *pid, Bool is_remove);
  ```
  Wired as `.configure_pid` of the `rfmpgvid` filter register by retained code later in this file; the filter core invokes it on input PID connection, reconfiguration, and removal. No other caller.
- **Observable behavior:** Establishes the filter'"'"'s single input PID, selects MPEG-1/2 vs MPEG-4 Part 2 handling, adopts input timing, and creates the framed output PID when the input provides a timescale.
- **Inputs:** The filter instance; the PID being connected/removed with `is_remove`; PID properties `GF_PROP_PID_TIMESCALE`, `GF_PROP_PID_FPS`, `GF_PROP_PID_CODECID`, `GF_PROP_PID_MIME`, `GF_PROP_PID_FILE_EXT`, boolean property `nocts`; filter argument `fps`.
- **Outputs and errors:** `GF_OK` after connect or removal; `GF_NOT_SUPPORTED` when the PID fails the filter'"'"'s capability negotiation, with no state mutated.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Stores the input PID; the working frame rate becomes the `fps` argument, defaulting to 25000/1000 when either term is zero. A timescale property is adopted as the output timescale and as the frame-rate numerator with zero denominator, replaced entirely by the FPS property when present; a true `nocts` sets the CTS-recompute flag. The MPEG-1/2 indication is set when a codec id property is present and is MPEG-1 or one of the MPEG-2 ids; otherwise, with no codec id property, when MIME contains `m1v`/`m2v`; else when the file extension does; its previous value is kept otherwise. An existing MPEG parser instance is discarded, its bitstream kept, when that indication changed. When a timescale was adopted and no output PID exists yet, the output PID is created, all input properties are copied onto it, and `GF_PROP_PID_UNFRAMED` is cleared. Removal forgets the input PID and removes the output PID if present.
- **Required sequencing and state:** The removal branch returns before touching other state; the capability failure returns before any state change; parser discard follows the classification comparison; output PID creation is the last step.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained — the range spans the whole function definition; retained text above ends the context struct and retained text below begins the next function, so nothing is left open. Mechanical consequence of the cut: the retained register struct further down references `mpgviddmx_configure_pid`, so that exact name and signature must be in scope when the region is restored.
