## Reached at
  The Composer CLI staged at /app by the image build: the composer/composer
  source tree cloned at tag 2.7.6 with its runtime dependencies installed
  in-tree during the build; no other Composer installation remains in the
  image. Callers drive the entry point by absolute path under the PHP
  interpreter, with the caller'"'"'s working directory set to a project directory:

      subprocess.run(["/usr/local/bin/php", "/app/bin/composer", *args],
                     cwd=<project directory>, env=<caller-built env dict>, ...)

  /app/bin/composer and the code it loads under /app are project-owned.
  /usr/local/bin/php (PHP 8.1), /usr/bin/git, and /bin/sh are preexisting
  system dependencies; the /tests tree is caller-owned.

## Must provide
  /app/bin/composer           CLI entry script, executable under
                              /usr/local/bin/php
  --version                   top-level option
  install                     subcommand; accepts --prefer-source and -n;
                              reads composer.json from the working directory
  status                      subcommand; accepts -v
  show                        subcommand; accepts -s and --format=json
  source-package status       surface reached from `status` when a dependency
                              was installed from git source: consults the
                              branch, remote-tracking refs under
                              refs/remotes/, and commit history of the package
                              checkout under vendor/
  root version guess          surface reached from any subcommand — callers
                              reach it through both `status` and `show` — when
                              the working-directory composer.json has no
                              "version" key and COMPOSER_ROOT_VERSION is
                              unset: consults the git state of the working
                              directory, and consults an `hg` program found on
                              PATH when the working directory is not a git
                              checkout

## Called as
  /usr/local/bin/php /app/bin/composer --version
      no further arguments.

  /usr/local/bin/php /app/bin/composer install --prefer-source -n
      working directory contains a composer.json: a JSON object with "name"
      (string), "require" (object mapping a package-name string to a
      version-constraint string), "repositories" (a list of objects, each with
      "type" a string and "url" a string — callers pass a local directory path
      as the URL), and "minimum-stability" (string).

  /usr/local/bin/php /app/bin/composer status -v
  /usr/local/bin/php /app/bin/composer status
      working directory is a project whose package checkout under
      vendor/<vendor>/<package> is a git checkout; its branch names,
      remote-tracking refs, and commits are caller-controlled; branch names
      are strings.

  /usr/local/bin/php /app/bin/composer show -s --format=json
      working directory contains a composer.json with no "version" key; the
      directory is either a git checkout (the checked-out branch name is a
      string; other local branch names are strings) or a non-git directory, in
      which case an `hg` program found on PATH is consulted for branch
      information.

  Every invocation receives an environment dict of strings:
  COMPOSER_ALLOW_SUPERUSER and COMPOSER_NO_INTERACTION are set,
  COMPOSER_ROOT_VERSION is absent, and PATH may be prefixed with a
  caller-owned directory.

## Setup required
  - PHP 8.1 at /usr/local/bin/php; Composer'"'"'s runtime dependencies under /app
    are installed by the image build, and the entry point must remain runnable
    with them.
  - git at /usr/bin/git with globally configured user.name/user.email (image-
    provided); callers create all repositories, branches, refs, and commits
    themselves.
  - Every invocation is working-directory sensitive: composer.json, .git, and
    vendor/ are read from the caller'"'"'s cwd.
  - For the source-package status surface, the caller has first run
    `install --prefer-source` in the same working directory.
  - The hg surface depends on PATH dispatch: the caller places its own
    executable named `hg` first on PATH, and the CLI resolves external `git`
    and `hg` programs from PATH.
  - The root-version-guess surface is only reached when the working-directory
    composer.json has no "version" key and COMPOSER_ROOT_VERSION is absent
    from the subprocess environment.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner drives the CLI as a subprocess, constructing each
  environment and working directory itself. All project directories, git
  repositories, branches, refs, and commits are created by the caller in
  temporary directories. For the hg surface the caller supplies its own `hg`
  executable — a shell script that reports caller-chosen branch names from an
  environment variable — and prefixes PATH with the directory holding it. That
  stub, and everything else under the caller-owned /tests tree, is not part of
  the implementation and must not be rebuilt.
